{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12525-pc-pantheons","id":12525,"title":"PC Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-16T22:27:37-08:00","id":12525,"title":"PC Pantheons","content":"I have been toying with the idea of my players making their own Pantheon when they manage to make it to being deities.<br /> <br /> I have not read any rules on this and I was wanting input on if this is a good idea or bad idea or if anyone has tried it and if so, what were their experiences with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T04:39:36-08:00","id":12656,"title":"","content":"I would do it probably to be the very last story arc to be played. It becomes kind of hard to follow it up and allows the players to reach the <i>status quo</i> of the other Pantheons.<br /> <br /> Here is an ordered list of things I would have them do:<br /> 1) Gather a group of Gods that might be interested in raising their own Legend and become much more important that they currently are, because a Pantheon isn't 5 newish Gods. This might include some Titan Avatars that are interested in becoming Gods, but I wouldn't recommend it, because it would upset the Titans and the Gods.<br /> <br /> 2) Gather a group of minor races to serve the new Pantheon, ones that aren't particularly liked by the other Pantheons is a good idea, for there is little interest for having them around and they might enjoy a better position of power. No other Pantheon would complain about some of their problems disappearing.<br /> <br /> 3) Carve their own Underworld, for there needs to be a place for the ghosts of those who believe in your new Pantheon to go rest. This should be fairly simple, for there is a lot of unused Underworld between the ones that the current Pantheons are using.<br /> <br /> 4) Place the future God of the Underworld building a proper Underworld realm to accommodate the future dead. I recommend an NPC, for it can be something the whole group isn't interested and should happen in the background. That God should have the Death Purview Avatar, but isn't required.<br /> <br /> 5) Carve their own Godrealm, for there needs to be a place for the gods to rule from. This is fairly more complicated, because the Overworld has between the current Godrealms the Greater Titans, which means the new Pantheon would have to fight at least one of them. Fighting a Grater Titan that is the major threat to a Godrealm would perhaps be the easiest choice, but I think it would be much more cooler to carve the Godrealm from an unknown Greater Titan (and allows you to fine tune the opposition). If the new Pantheon choses to attack a known Greater Titan, I would say that an unknown Greater Titan Allied with the one they attacked to be the major threat to the new Pantheon.<br /> <br /> 6) Build the Infrastructure that the Godrealm requires, bring the minor races to help defend the Godrealm from the Titan Threat. The Gods need somewhere to live, to do their proper work... Anything you want is fine, but don't forget about a couple Axis Mundi.<br /> <br /> 7) Become Fatebound to a lot of people, because humans need to know about their Legend. Going to Earth and doing something as an Purview Avatar works pretty well, you can even start a new religion and a nation this way. Don't push it so far that it is a threat to the other Pantheons or the Greater Titan can take advantage from your absence from the new Godrealm.<br /> <br /> 8) Summon the Wyrd (the Fate Purviews Avatar), so that the new Pantheon is recognized by Fate due to their deeds. They gathered allies, carved an Underworld for their dead to live on, carved an Godrealm for them to live, are fighting a Grater Titan that opposes them, are Fatebound by a lot of people who are in tune with their legend already... Here I would tally up how they rate in their Virtues and pick the 4 highest to be their Pantheon Virtues and would (with the players) develop a Pantheon Purview that is in tune with their deeds and fate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I had this story planned, so I'm going to tell you how I would do it for my Game. Hopefully it will give you ideas for what you want:<br /> 1) Since they were still Demigods when the game ended, there wasn't much contact with the Gods besides bossing them around. The exception was the God of the Last Breath (currently living in Yomi, the Japanese Underworld). Another notable mention is Circe, who fell in love with the group's pretty boy, and could become a Goddess in her own right for she is the daughter of known Titan Avatars. I also had intentions to approach the Vanir to ally with the new Pantheon, as a new faction, but never got around on how to make it work without upsetting the Aesir.<br /> <br /> 2) Previously the Scions turned some Dwarves into stone and because of it were forced to find a stone which granted life to realistic sculptures, so that the Dwarves might live again. This unfortunately resulted in the Dwarves turned to stone to become living stone dwarves, immune to the sunlight. Some Dwarves took the chance to live outside and exposed to the sun and voluntarily became part of the Stone Dwarves faction, who live away from humans, but can stand the power of the sun. I also had intentions to exploit this connection to approach the Svartalfar into alliance.<br /> <br /> 3-4) Since none of the players were interested in Death, the God of the Last Breath would become the new God of the Underworld and would take the uninhabited part of the Underworld and shape it to his liking. Something akin to Malfeas from Exalted (since I based my God of the Last Breath as similar to Ligier).<br /> <br /> 5-6) I had the bare bones of the Greater Titan of Wrath (based on the Chaos Realm of Khorne from Warhammer), it would only have a single Titan Avatar that was in a similar position of power and influence to that of Aten. The Greater Titan would have Favored: War, Chaos, Death, Fire; and Banned: Justice, Guardian. The realm was all red, blood, lava, broken lands, brass... there was sufficient to produce a Titanrealm from which it was possible to produce a Godrealm from.<br /> <br /> 7-8) Similar thoughts as the ones mentioned above. For the Pantheon Purview, the players had themes around shapeshifting and transmuting things and transcending their natural state, so their Pantheon Purview would play around those notions.<br /> <br /> As you can see, I only had the bare bones of this story, but at the time I thought it there was plenty of time to get there. Hopefully this helps and if you want any help, I wouldn't mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","user":"Man in Black","date":". 11-17-2013, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T04:46:38-08:00","id":12659,"title":"","content":"I already have them doing battle with the minions of a Greater Titan who they will fight at the climax of the chronicle. So, most of those steps could be done prior to that. They just need to ally with (and stop alienating) the other Scions that they meet. Although, they do know someone who would be the perfect Death God. He is a zombie that I brought in using an old fan-game called Zombie: the Coil.<br /> <br /> If you find that story, then go ahead and post it on here or PM it to me. Whatever you feel more comfortable with. I know that my players do come to the forums so I need to be vague about what I post on here in regards to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T04:47:28-08:00","id":12660,"title":"","content":"Many thanks to you both. I know that this question will come up soon in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T06:08:55-08:00","id":12682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/