ection to approach the Svartalfar into alliance.<br /> <br /> 3-4) Since none of the players were interested in Death, the God of the Last Breath would become the new God of the Underworld and would take the uninhabited part of the Underworld and shape it to his liking. Something akin to Malfeas from Exalted (since I based my God of the Last Breath as similar to Ligier).<br /> <br /> 5-6) I had the bare bones of the Greater Titan of Wrath (based on the Chaos Realm of Khorne from Warhammer), it would only have a single Titan Avatar that was in a similar position of power and influence to that of Aten. The Greater Titan would have Favored: War, Chaos, Death, Fire; and Banned: Justice, Guardian. The realm was all red, blood, lava, broken lands, brass... there was sufficient to produce a Titanrealm from which it was possible to produce a Godrealm from.<br /> <br /> 7-8) Similar thoughts as the ones mentioned above. For the Pantheon Purview, the players had themes around shapeshifting and transmuting things and transcending their natural state, so their Pantheon Purview would play around those notions.<br /> <br /> As you can see, I only had the bare bones of this story, but at the time I thought it there was plenty of time to get there. Hopefully this helps and if you want any help, I wouldn't mind.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:11:45-08:00","id":14385,"title":"","content":"Founding a new Pantheon should be akin to (and possibly linked with) founding a new nation, or at least a new religion. I\u2019d handle the \u201ccarving out your own Godrealm/Underworld\u201d as being tasks that are enabled through Fatebinding of mortal worshippers, turning their holy sites into Axes Mundi that connect to a previously unknown Godrealm and Underworld. The newly-discovered Godrealm can also be a source of servant races and/or Titans, depending on whether they end up aligned to or opposing the new Pantheon. On the subject of Titans, I\u2019d say that establishing a new Pantheon attracts the attention of the Greater Titans, and potentially spawns new Avatars within them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T04:04:15-08:00","id":14643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12525-pc-pantheons?p=14385#post14385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Founding a new Pantheon should be akin to (and possibly linked with) founding a new nation, or at least a new religion. I\u2019d handle the \u201ccarving out your own Godrealm/Underworld\u201d as being tasks that are enabled through Fatebinding of mortal worshippers, turning their holy sites into Axes Mundi that connect to a previously unknown Godrealm and Underworld. The newly-discovered Godrealm can also be a source of servant races and/or Titans, depending on whether they end up aligned to or opposing the new Pantheon. On the subject of Titans, I\u2019d say that establishing a new Pantheon attracts the attention of the Greater Titans, and potentially spawns new Avatars within them.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree this should be part of the process of making a new Pantheon, I must disagree that it should be the only one. It ties too much to Fate and what silly things mortals tell about what happens in a World full of Gods, leaving all to the ST to decide, which could lead to the ST making decisions that don't please most of the players because &quot;it is what people think, they saw you riding a dragon once, so now you are their Dragon God, gain Animal (dragon) and you look somewhat like a dragon&quot;.<br /> <br /> In my view of Fatebinding, where mortals are pulled into a God's preexisting legend and enforce the concepts in that legend, it makes more sense to have all the hard work done by the players before messing around with Fate, for it is a misunderstood thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T08:15:55-08:00","id":14710,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m certainly open to there being more to it than <i>just</i> Fatebinding. As you say, scions define their legends; which puts the responsibility of determining what the Godrealm will be like at least in part in the players\u2019 hands. <br /> <br /> That said, I have no problem with leaving at least some aspects in the Storyteller\u2019s hands, with the caveat that the Storyteller is expected to workwith the players toward an end result that everyone finds acceptable. The players can describe to the Storyteller what they\u2019re after from their GodRealm, and the Storyteller can technically use it, elaborate on it, change it, or ignore it as he chooses; but a wise Storyteller will lean heavily toward the former options: it doesn\u2019t pay to unnecesarily antagonize your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T11:17:22-08:00","id":14796,"title":"","content":"Any word whether or not rules such as these will actually be included in the new supplement for God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T13:19:50-08:00","id":17267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12525-pc-pantheons?p=14796#post14796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any word whether or not rules such as these will actually be included in the new supplement for God?</div> </div> </div> </div>Current plan for <b>Demigod</b> is to have mechanics on how pantheons are formed or re-formed (<i>interpretatio romana)</i>. Kind of stands to reason that PCs could take advantage of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T18:25:24-08:00","id":17422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12525-pc-pantheons?p=17267#post17267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Current plan for <b>Demigod</b> is to have mechanics on how pantheons are formed or re-formed (<i>interpretatio romana)</i>. Kind of stands to reason that PCs could take advantage of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will it specifically address newly-minted gods, Neall? I think that's more the desire; something aimed specifically at a PC group looking to set up their own shop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/cor